1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,550
What's today's video about? Everyone's favorite—summer vacation!

2
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:17,129
At some point in the video, a question will pop up in Japanese. If you hear it, leave a comment!

3
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:20,879
Scene 1: Morning Radio Calisthenics

4
00:00:20,879 --> 00:00:23,879
Hey, big brother, wake up!

5
00:00:23,901 --> 00:00:24,325
It's already 5:30 in the morning.

6
00:00:24,325 --> 00:00:27,691
I'm still sleepy...

7
00:00:27,714 --> 00:00:32,848
Summer vacation's here, sis—why are we waking up so early?

8
00:00:32,871 --> 00:00:36,837
Radio calisthenics starts this morning!

9
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,759
We’ll be late if we don’t hurry.

10
00:00:38,783 --> 00:00:42,063
Radio calisthenics, huh?

11
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:44,544
Feels nostalgic.

12
00:00:44,567 --> 00:00:47,850
But I’m not going.

13
00:00:47,874 --> 00:00:52,907
Come on, you promised we’d go together!

14
00:00:52,930 --> 00:00:55,963
Did I?

15
00:00:55,986 --> 00:00:59,031
Just let me sleep 10 more minutes...

16
00:00:59,055 --> 00:01:04,222
Get up! We need to get our stamp card.

17
00:01:04,245 --> 00:01:06,778
Stamp card?

18
00:01:06,801 --> 00:01:11,297
If we collect a bunch, do we get something good?

19
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:15,860
On the last day, they give out snacks and notebooks!

20
00:01:15,884 --> 00:01:19,292
Oh, that’s cool.

21
00:01:19,316 --> 00:01:22,749
Just like when we were kids.

22
00:01:22,772 --> 00:01:26,189
So hurry up and get ready!

23
00:01:26,212 --> 00:01:29,857
It takes 10 minutes to walk to the park.

24
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:32,548
Alright, alright...

25
00:01:32,571 --> 00:01:35,051
I’m up, I’m up.

26
00:01:35,074 --> 00:01:37,749
Go wash your face quickly!

27
00:01:37,772 --> 00:01:41,351
I’ll put on my shoes and wait for you.

28
00:01:41,374 --> 00:01:44,426
Is it already hot outside?

29
00:01:44,449 --> 00:01:46,116
Nope.

30
00:01:46,139 --> 00:01:49,972
There’s a breeze—it’s nice and cool in the morning.

31
00:01:49,995 --> 00:01:52,029
Feels great.

32
00:01:52,052 --> 00:01:55,525
Then let’s hurry!

33
00:01:55,548 --> 00:02:00,127
Do you still remember the radio calisthenics music?

34
00:02:00,151 --> 00:02:04,249
I practiced at school, so I’m good.

35
00:02:04,272 --> 00:02:07,039
I’ll teach you.

36
00:02:07,062 --> 00:02:08,434
Thanks.

37
00:02:08,457 --> 00:02:12,024
Okay, I’m ready—let’s go!

38
00:02:12,047 --> 00:02:15,880
Oh, don’t forget the stamp card!

39
00:02:15,903 --> 00:02:18,115
Whoa, almost forgot!

40
00:02:18,139 --> 00:02:20,739
It was on the desk.

41
00:02:20,762 --> 00:02:23,729
Alright, let’s head out!

42
00:02:23,752 --> 00:02:30,857
A link to review today’s video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

43
00:02:30,857 --> 00:02:33,857
Scene 2: Summer Pool Opening and the Dreaded Cold Shower

44
00:02:33,857 --> 00:02:37,890
Want to go to the school pool this afternoon?

45
00:02:37,913 --> 00:02:39,720
Sounds good!

46
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:43,635
The summer pool opens today, right?

47
00:02:43,659 --> 00:02:44,938
Yep!

48
00:02:44,961 --> 00:02:51,194
It starts at 1 PM, so let’s meet at the school gate at 12:30.

49
00:02:51,217 --> 00:02:52,584
Got it.

50
00:02:52,607 --> 00:02:57,426
But that first shower is *freezing*, isn’t it?

51
00:02:57,449 --> 00:03:01,683
Ah, the infamous 'hellish shower,' huh?

52
00:03:01,706 --> 00:03:05,590
It’s so cold—I really don’t like it.

53
00:03:05,613 --> 00:03:09,946
But we *have* to take it for disinfection.

54
00:03:09,969 --> 00:03:12,703
Did you bring your cap and goggles?

55
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:14,165
Yep.

56
00:03:14,188 --> 00:03:16,189
I packed them in my bag.

57
00:03:16,212 --> 00:03:18,546
Got my towel ready too.

58
00:03:18,569 --> 00:03:22,702
The weather’s nice, so the water should feel great.

59
00:03:22,725 --> 00:03:28,202
I was worried we might not get to go today since it rained yesterday.

60
00:03:28,226 --> 00:03:33,159
It’s so hot today—no way we’re skipping it.

61
00:03:33,182 --> 00:03:37,790
After swimming, I want something cold to eat.

62
00:03:37,813 --> 00:03:42,854
Let’s grab ice cream at the convenience store near school.

63
00:03:42,877 --> 00:03:45,044
That sounds perfect.

64
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:47,700
Better bring some spending money.

65
00:03:47,723 --> 00:03:52,157
Do we have to swim quietly in the pool?

66
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:57,659
The teachers will be watching, so if we make too much noise, we’ll get scolded.

67
00:03:57,683 --> 00:03:59,749
Got it, I’ll be careful.

68
00:03:59,772 --> 00:04:02,047
See you later, then.

69
00:04:02,071 --> 00:04:03,304
Yep.

70
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:06,094
Meet you at the gate at 12:30.

71
00:04:06,117 --> 00:04:08,093
Don’t be late!

72
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:09,450
No worries.

73
00:04:09,473 --> 00:04:12,141
I’ll rush there by bike.

74
00:04:12,164 --> 00:04:21,846
If you could hear me, leave a comment!

75
00:04:21,846 --> 00:04:24,846
Scene 3: The Chaos of Obon Holiday Travel

76
00:04:24,846 --> 00:04:29,126
Obon break starts next week, right?

77
00:04:29,149 --> 00:04:33,149
Are you going anywhere, senpai?

78
00:04:33,172 --> 00:04:38,442
I’m heading back to my hometown.

79
00:04:38,466 --> 00:04:41,899
I booked a Shinkansen ticket.

80
00:04:41,922 --> 00:04:43,927
That’s nice.

81
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:49,040
Was it easy to get the Shinkansen tickets?

82
00:04:49,063 --> 00:04:52,230
Not at all.

83
00:04:52,253 --> 00:04:57,292
Obon season is always a nightmare.

84
00:04:57,315 --> 00:05:05,515
I saw on the news that trains can get packed to 200% capacity.

85
00:05:05,538 --> 00:05:07,538
Yeah, they do.

86
00:05:07,561 --> 00:05:13,830
The unreserved cars get so crowded you can barely move.

87
00:05:13,854 --> 00:05:20,254
I’ve never experienced Obon traffic in Japan before.

88
00:05:20,277 --> 00:05:28,844
Highways get backed up for like 40 kilometers—driving home is rough too.

89
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:32,004
That’s insane.

90
00:05:32,027 --> 00:05:37,294
Why does everyone go home at the same time?

91
00:05:37,317 --> 00:05:41,884
Because companies all give time off at once.

92
00:05:41,907 --> 00:05:45,281
There’s nothing we can do about it.

93
00:05:45,304 --> 00:05:50,471
What do you do with your family back home?

94
00:05:50,494 --> 00:05:56,974
Visit the family grave, meet up with old friends for meals—that kind of thing.

95
00:05:56,998 --> 00:05:59,464
Sounds fun.

96
00:05:59,487 --> 00:06:04,130
I’ll have to bring back lots of souvenirs.

97
00:06:04,154 --> 00:06:08,609
I’m planning to get those famous Tokyo cookies.

98
00:06:08,632 --> 00:06:14,565
Your parents back home must be excited to see you.

99
00:06:14,588 --> 00:06:17,022
Hope so.

100
00:06:17,045 --> 00:06:21,078
What about you? What are your plans for summer break?

101
00:06:21,101 --> 00:06:26,999
I’m not going anywhere—just relaxing in Tokyo.

102
00:06:27,022 --> 00:06:30,194
That sounds good too.

103
00:06:30,217 --> 00:06:35,217
Tokyo is so quiet during Obon because there are fewer people around.

104
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,490
Really?

105
00:06:37,514 --> 00:06:42,181
Then let’s go grab something delicious to eat.

106
00:06:42,204 --> 00:06:44,237
Sounds good!

107
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:48,994
Let’s talk about souvenirs when we’re back from break.

108
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:52,017
Take care while you’re away.

109
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:55,040
Scene 4: Summer in the Countryside – Watermelons and Offline Life

110
00:06:55,040 --> 00:07:00,573
Grandpa’s place in the countryside is so peaceful.

111
00:07:00,596 --> 00:07:03,974
All I can hear is the sound of wind chimes.

112
00:07:03,997 --> 00:07:06,630
This is actually nice once in a while.

113
00:07:06,653 --> 00:07:11,231
But there’s no Wi-Fi signal here at all.

114
00:07:11,255 --> 00:07:14,588
I can’t even watch videos on my phone.

115
00:07:14,611 --> 00:07:17,545
Well, we *are* near the mountains.

116
00:07:17,568 --> 00:07:22,034
Why not take a break from the internet and just relax for once?

117
00:07:22,057 --> 00:07:26,191
There’s nothing to do—I’m so bored.

118
00:07:26,214 --> 00:07:29,419
All I can do is lie around on the tatami.

119
00:07:29,442 --> 00:07:33,809
Then how about some watermelon Grandma cut for us?

120
00:07:33,832 --> 00:07:36,724
Oh, that looks delicious!

121
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:39,481
It’s so cold and sweet.

122
00:07:39,504 --> 00:07:45,537
Eating watermelon on the veranda—this really feels like a Japanese summer, doesn’t it?

123
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,216
Yep.

124
00:07:47,239 --> 00:07:50,696
Hey, what’s that smoke coming from in the garden?

125
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:55,120
Oh, that’s mosquito coil.

126
00:07:55,143 --> 00:07:57,676
It keeps the mosquitoes away.

127
00:07:57,699 --> 00:08:00,666
It has a pretty unique smell.

128
00:08:00,689 --> 00:08:04,422
But it’s kinda soothing, actually.

129
00:08:04,445 --> 00:08:09,378
Later, let’s go to the river nearby.

130
00:08:09,401 --> 00:08:10,368
The river?

131
00:08:10,391 --> 00:08:12,484
Can we swim there?

132
00:08:12,507 --> 00:08:14,507
Yeah, we can.

133
00:08:14,531 --> 00:08:19,331
The water’s super clear and refreshing.

134
00:08:19,354 --> 00:08:20,958
I wanna go!

135
00:08:20,981 --> 00:08:23,181
Are there fish too?

136
00:08:23,204 --> 00:08:26,470
There are tons of little fish.

137
00:08:26,493 --> 00:08:29,633
If we’re lucky, we might even catch some.

138
00:08:29,657 --> 00:08:31,390
I can’t wait!

139
00:08:31,413 --> 00:08:36,746
I thought the countryside would be boring, but there’s actually a lot to do.

140
00:08:36,769 --> 00:08:38,742
Exactly.

141
00:08:38,766 --> 00:08:44,017
At night, the stars are incredible—you’ll love that too.

142
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:49,933
You can’t see stars like this in Tokyo, so I’m really looking forward to it.

143
00:08:49,957 --> 00:08:54,490
Well, I might take a nap while I can.

144
00:08:54,513 --> 00:08:57,513
Scene 5: Preparing for Summer Tennis Camp and Concerns

145
00:08:57,513 --> 00:09:02,970
Tennis club’s summer camp starts next week.

146
00:09:02,994 --> 00:09:07,483
Ugh, just thinking about it makes me depressed.

147
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:11,772
We’ll be practicing from morning till night every day.

148
00:09:11,795 --> 00:09:17,040
This year’s camp is at the courts up in the mountains, right?

149
00:09:17,064 --> 00:09:24,339
Yeah. It *might* be a little cooler up there, but the courts will still be scorching.

150
00:09:24,362 --> 00:09:30,538
I heard the upperclassmen get way stricter during camp.

151
00:09:30,561 --> 00:09:33,129
Oh, they do.

152
00:09:33,153 --> 00:09:38,886
The night meetings drag on forever, and there’s no free time at all.

153
00:09:38,909 --> 00:09:42,243
Have you finished packing yet?

154
00:09:42,266 --> 00:09:43,799
Yep.

155
00:09:43,822 --> 00:09:49,028
Yeah. I packed three rackets and a bunch of practice clothes in my bag.

156
00:09:49,051 --> 00:09:56,334
I'm worried about heatstroke, so I'm bringing lots of sports drink powder.

157
00:09:56,358 --> 00:09:59,396
That's a good idea.

158
00:09:59,419 --> 00:10:05,490
We really need to drink plenty of fluids during training camp—it's dangerous otherwise.

159
00:10:05,514 --> 00:10:08,114
I wonder if the food will be good?

160
00:10:08,137 --> 00:10:12,403
I heard the meals at the inn are really filling.

161
00:10:12,426 --> 00:10:15,840
We’ve got to eat a lot or we won’t have the stamina.

162
00:10:15,864 --> 00:10:22,712
Practice is tough, but sleeping in the same room with everyone at night sounds fun.

163
00:10:22,736 --> 00:10:27,190
Well, I think we’ll be so tired we’ll pass out right away.

164
00:10:27,213 --> 00:10:30,379
True.

165
00:10:30,402 --> 00:10:35,402
True. But after training camp, we’ll all be better, right?

166
00:10:35,425 --> 00:10:38,859
We’ve just got to believe that and push through.

167
00:10:38,882 --> 00:10:41,523
I want to win our matches.

168
00:10:41,546 --> 00:10:43,146
Yep.

169
00:10:43,170 --> 00:10:46,903
Let’s get through this tough training together.

170
00:10:46,926 --> 00:10:50,404
Alright, let’s psych ourselves up!

171
00:10:50,428 --> 00:10:54,561
First, let’s double-check so we don’t forget anything.

172
00:10:54,584 --> 00:10:57,799
Don’t forget sunscreen!

173
00:10:57,823 --> 00:11:00,423
Oh, I forgot about that!

174
00:11:00,446 --> 00:11:03,025
Thanks for reminding me.

175
00:11:03,049 --> 00:11:06,049
Scene 6: The Summer Battle – Exam Season Crunch

176
00:11:06,049 --> 00:11:12,538
It’s only 8 AM—how is the cram school’s study room already packed?

177
00:11:12,562 --> 00:11:19,362
Everyone’s using their summer break to study early in the morning.

178
00:11:19,385 --> 00:11:22,682
Exam students are really going all out.

179
00:11:22,705 --> 00:11:26,315
Where should we study, then?

180
00:11:26,338 --> 00:11:29,971
Let’s try the library nearby.

181
00:11:29,994 --> 00:11:34,034
It’s quiet there, and we might find seats.

182
00:11:34,058 --> 00:11:36,143
Yeah.

183
00:11:36,166 --> 00:11:42,533
There are so many distractions at home during summer break—I can’t focus at all.

184
00:11:42,556 --> 00:11:44,805
I know what you mean.

185
00:11:44,828 --> 00:11:49,276
I want to watch TV and play games, too.

186
00:11:49,299 --> 00:11:55,366
The summer courses at cram school—three classes every day—are exhausting.

187
00:11:55,389 --> 00:12:01,956
Our teacher said, ‘Summer is the decisive battle for exams.’ I remember that now.

188
00:12:01,979 --> 00:12:04,867
What does ‘decisive battle’ mean?

189
00:12:04,891 --> 00:12:09,457
It means it’s the most important time.

190
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:13,373
If we don’t push hard now, we won’t pass.

191
00:12:13,397 --> 00:12:15,632
I see.

192
00:12:15,656 --> 00:12:18,889
Are you ready for today’s test?

193
00:12:18,912 --> 00:12:24,979
No, I didn’t finish reviewing yesterday’s material—I’m a little worried.

194
00:12:25,002 --> 00:12:31,376
Once we get to the library, let’s help each other with what we don’t understand.

195
00:12:31,399 --> 00:12:33,067
That’d be a huge help.

196
00:12:33,091 --> 00:12:38,491
I’m especially struggling with memorizing math formulas.

197
00:12:38,514 --> 00:12:42,681
I can help with math.

198
00:12:42,704 --> 00:12:46,037
In return, teach me English.

199
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:47,545
Deal.

200
00:12:47,569 --> 00:12:51,702
I’ll show you some tips for reading comprehension in English.

201
00:12:51,725 --> 00:12:53,459
Alright!

202
00:12:53,482 --> 00:12:56,016
Let’s hurry to the library.

203
00:12:56,039 --> 00:12:59,732
Just walking makes me sweat.

204
00:12:59,756 --> 00:13:02,522
It’s so hot.

205
00:13:02,545 --> 00:13:06,236
I can’t wait to get into an air-conditioned room.

206
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:10,137
Let's grab a cold drink from the convenience store before we go.

207
00:13:10,161 --> 00:13:13,174
Staying hydrated is important, after all.

208
00:13:13,197 --> 00:13:16,197
Scene 7: Summer Vacation Travel Plans

209
00:13:16,197 --> 00:13:20,764
Should we go somewhere for summer vacation this year?

210
00:13:20,787 --> 00:13:22,853
Sounds good!

211
00:13:22,876 --> 00:13:29,610
It's my first summer break as a college student, so I want to go somewhere far.

212
00:13:29,633 --> 00:13:31,799
How about Hokkaido?

213
00:13:31,822 --> 00:13:35,389
I heard it's cool there even in the summer.

214
00:13:35,412 --> 00:13:37,845
Hokkaido, huh?

215
00:13:37,868 --> 00:13:39,556
Sounds good!

216
00:13:39,579 --> 00:13:43,388
There's so much delicious food there too.

217
00:13:43,412 --> 00:13:49,496
We should book our plane tickets soon, or they might get expensive.

218
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,320
Yep.

219
00:13:51,343 --> 00:13:59,556
Mid-August is pricey, so late July or early September would be better.

220
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:02,913
How about the last week of July?

221
00:14:02,936 --> 00:14:05,936
That's right after our exams end.

222
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:11,209
We might still get cheap tickets if we book for then.

223
00:14:11,232 --> 00:14:16,632
Once we get to Hokkaido, let's rent a car and go for a drive.

224
00:14:16,655 --> 00:14:22,857
I just got my license, so driving makes me a little nervous.

225
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:25,514
Don't worry.

226
00:14:25,537 --> 00:14:31,737
A senior told me the roads in Hokkaido are wide and easy to drive on.

227
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:34,395
That's reassuring.

228
00:14:34,419 --> 00:14:38,552
I'd love to see the lavender fields in Furano.

229
00:14:38,575 --> 00:14:40,808
They must be beautiful.

230
00:14:40,832 --> 00:14:45,565
For dinner, let's have Genghis Khan (grilled lamb) and ramen.

231
00:14:45,588 --> 00:14:48,990
I definitely want to try seafood bowls too.

232
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:51,686
I'm getting hungry just thinking about it.

233
00:14:51,710 --> 00:14:55,162
How much do you think we'll need for the budget?

234
00:14:55,186 --> 00:15:00,219
Around 50,000 yen for flights and hotels, I think.

235
00:15:00,242 --> 00:15:04,209
I need to work part-time and save up.

236
00:15:04,232 --> 00:15:08,965
I plan to pick up a lot of shifts this month too.

237
00:15:08,988 --> 00:15:14,156
I'll send you some hotel options on LINE tonight.

238
00:15:14,179 --> 00:15:15,913
Thanks!

239
00:15:15,936 --> 00:15:18,508
I can't wait!

240
00:15:18,532 --> 00:15:21,532
Scene 8: The Reality of Working at a Beach Hut

241
00:15:21,532 --> 00:15:25,765
Have you decided on your summer job yet?

242
00:15:25,788 --> 00:15:27,355
Yep.

243
00:15:27,379 --> 00:15:31,251
I'm going to work at a beach hut.

244
00:15:31,275 --> 00:15:34,127
It's a live-in job.

245
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,317
That sounds amazing!

246
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:41,789
Working at a beach hut means you get to see the ocean every day. It must be fun.

247
00:15:41,812 --> 00:15:48,979
That's what I thought when I applied, but it's actually pretty tough.

248
00:15:49,002 --> 00:15:51,935
What kind of work will you be doing?

249
00:15:51,958 --> 00:16:00,228
I'll be cooking for customers, selling shaved ice, and renting out parasols.

250
00:16:00,251 --> 00:16:04,690
Will you be outside from morning till night?

251
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:08,533
Yeah.

252
00:16:08,556 --> 00:16:12,723
A senior told me it's super hot every day, and you get really sunburned.

253
00:16:12,746 --> 00:16:17,027
But you must earn a lot of money, right?

254
00:16:17,051 --> 00:16:18,617
Yep.

255
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:23,007
I'm expecting to make around 200,000 yen in a month.

256
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:26,075
That's enviable!

257
00:16:26,099 --> 00:16:30,902
I'm going to work at a café nearby.

258
00:16:30,925 --> 00:16:35,059
A café with air conditioning sounds nice.

259
00:16:35,082 --> 00:16:42,891
But it gets really busy during lunchtime, and I'll be on my feet all day. It's exhausting.

260
00:16:42,915 --> 00:16:48,648
Every job has its own challenges, doesn't it?

261
00:16:48,671 --> 00:16:50,683
Yeah.

262
00:16:50,706 --> 00:16:55,078
When does the beach shack part-time job start?

263
00:16:55,101 --> 00:16:59,068
It starts next Monday.

264
00:16:59,091 --> 00:17:03,499
I'm packing my things and leaving tomorrow.

265
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:06,989
Take care of yourself and good luck!

266
00:17:07,013 --> 00:17:10,791
I can't wait to hear all about your adventures.

267
00:17:10,814 --> 00:17:12,547
Thanks!

268
00:17:12,570 --> 00:17:16,374
I'll come back with a serious tan.

269
00:17:16,397 --> 00:17:19,197
Come visit me at the café sometime!

270
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:23,288
Of course, I'll drop by on my day off.

271
00:17:23,312 --> 00:17:26,312
Scene 9: The Last-Minute Summer Homework Struggle

272
00:17:26,312 --> 00:17:34,650
Hey, please, I'm begging you—send me a photo of the math workbook from page 35 to the end.

273
00:17:34,674 --> 00:17:35,807
Huh?

274
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:39,964
You still haven't finished your homework?

275
00:17:39,987 --> 00:17:44,443
It's August 31st today.

276
00:17:44,466 --> 00:17:47,324
I haven't even started.

277
00:17:47,347 --> 00:17:51,364
And I still have 10 kanji worksheets left.

278
00:17:51,388 --> 00:17:54,882
You do this every year.

279
00:17:54,905 --> 00:18:00,072
Even though you made such a solid plan at the start of summer.

280
00:18:00,095 --> 00:18:07,353
I tried hard the first week, but then I just slacked off the whole time.

281
00:18:07,376 --> 00:18:12,021
I finished everything a week ago.

282
00:18:12,044 --> 00:18:14,258
Wow, impressive.

283
00:18:14,282 --> 00:18:18,215
Please, just let me see the math answers.

284
00:18:18,238 --> 00:18:20,679
I just need to copy them.

285
00:18:20,703 --> 00:18:25,381
Copying answers won't help you learn.

286
00:18:25,405 --> 00:18:29,038
Desperate times call for desperate measures.

287
00:18:29,061 --> 00:18:33,794
If I don't turn it in tomorrow, my teacher will be furious.

288
00:18:33,817 --> 00:18:36,751
Fine, I guess I have no choice.

289
00:18:36,774 --> 00:18:40,707
Alright, I'll take a photo and send it to you now.

290
00:18:40,730 --> 00:18:43,497
Thank you so much. You're a lifesaver!

291
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:45,920
You're like an angel right now.

292
00:18:45,943 --> 00:18:49,776
By the way, what about your illustrated diary?

293
00:18:49,799 --> 00:18:52,199
Do you remember the weather?

294
00:18:52,222 --> 00:18:56,257
I don't remember the weather at all.

295
00:18:56,281 --> 00:18:59,481
Maybe I'll just write 'sunny' for everything.

296
00:18:59,504 --> 00:19:05,970
You can look up past weather forecasts online, so check properly and write it down.

297
00:19:05,993 --> 00:19:09,435
Oh right, I never thought of that.

298
00:19:09,459 --> 00:19:12,225
I'll search for it now.

299
00:19:12,248 --> 00:19:14,782
Did you finish your independent research project?

300
00:19:14,805 --> 00:19:21,772
I bought a DIY kit that only takes a day to finish, so I'm good.

301
00:19:21,795 --> 00:19:24,734
You solved it with money, huh?

302
00:19:24,758 --> 00:19:27,728
Well, as long as it's done.

303
00:19:27,752 --> 00:19:31,752
Alright, time to pull an all-nighter!

304
00:19:31,775 --> 00:19:36,245
Just don't oversleep and be late tomorrow.

305
00:19:36,268 --> 00:19:39,041
Okay, I'm sending the photos now.

306
00:19:39,065 --> 00:19:42,065
Scene 10: Preparing for the New School Term

307
00:19:42,065 --> 00:19:43,998
Good morning.

308
00:19:44,021 --> 00:19:46,316
Long time no see!

309
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:49,033
New term starts today.

310
00:19:49,056 --> 00:19:50,874
Good morning.

311
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:55,132
Ugh, I'm not looking forward to going back to school.

312
00:19:55,155 --> 00:19:58,088
I'm still sleepy...

313
00:19:58,111 --> 00:19:59,946
Wait a minute...

314
00:19:59,969 --> 00:20:03,903
Is your hair okay?

315
00:20:03,926 --> 00:20:07,359
It's still a little brown.

316
00:20:07,382 --> 00:20:09,849
Oh no, seriously?

317
00:20:09,872 --> 00:20:16,045
I dyed it during summer break, but I fixed it with black hair spray. It should be fine.

318
00:20:16,068 --> 00:20:25,468
It looks pretty brown in the light. The discipline teacher is standing by the school gate.

319
00:20:25,491 --> 00:20:27,625
Oh wow, you're right.

320
00:20:27,648 --> 00:20:30,081
That's Mr. Tanaka.

321
00:20:30,104 --> 00:20:33,737
If he catches us, we're definitely in trouble.

322
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:38,452
We'll get dragged to the staff room and lectured.

323
00:20:38,476 --> 00:20:40,509
What should we do?

324
00:20:40,532 --> 00:20:45,466
I'll go to the bathroom and spray it again.

325
00:20:45,489 --> 00:20:49,855
You better hurry. The opening ceremony is about to start.

326
00:20:49,878 --> 00:20:53,645
Hey, is your skirt length okay?

327
00:20:53,668 --> 00:20:55,668
Isn't it too short?

328
00:20:55,691 --> 00:21:00,458
Oh, I shortened it during summer break.

329
00:21:00,481 --> 00:21:04,857
I just folded it with a belt, so I'll fix it now.

330
00:21:04,881 --> 00:21:09,447
We still haven't shaken off our summer vibes, huh?

331
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,470
Yeah, totally.

332
00:21:11,493 --> 00:21:16,327
School rules are strict, so we gotta be careful.

333
00:21:16,349 --> 00:21:19,816
Did you get your ears pierced?

334
00:21:19,839 --> 00:21:26,172
My friends did, but I was too scared to try.

335
00:21:26,196 --> 00:21:28,429
That's good.

336
00:21:28,452 --> 00:21:32,097
Piercings are an instant fail.

337
00:21:32,121 --> 00:21:35,521
Alright, I fixed my skirt length.

338
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:38,435
How's my hair?

339
00:21:38,458 --> 00:21:42,544
I wet it in the bathroom and tidied it up a bit.

340
00:21:42,568 --> 00:21:44,704
Do you think this is okay?

341
00:21:44,728 --> 00:21:48,967
Yeah, it looks darker than before.

342
00:21:48,991 --> 00:21:52,357
Let's hurry through the gate.

343
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:56,380
And avoid making eye contact with the teacher.